<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Hashim</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hashemites, clan of Hashim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banu Hashim was a clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a> tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, named after Hashim ibn Abd Manaf, the great-grandfather of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a>. It held the right to provide food and water for pilgrims to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a>. The Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> and many later dynasties, including the Hashemite kings of Jordan, claimed descent from it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banu-hashim.jpg" alt="Banu Hashim" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aziz911q8 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Name_of_Banu_Hashim.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
